hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"242","Kāna an-nabiyyu ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam idhā atāhu amrun yasurruhu aw yusarra bihi kharra sājidan shukran lillāhi tabāraka wa-taʿālā.. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) was given a matter that pleased him, or something joyful came to him, he would fall into prostration, out of gratitude to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted."
"243","Bismillāh (three times). Then say seven times: A`ūdhu billāhi wa qudratihi min sharri mā ajidu wa uḥādhir. Put your hand on the place where you feel pain and say: With the Name of Allah (three times). Then say seven times: I seek refuge in Allah and in His Power from the evil of what I find and of what I guard against. Reference: Muslim 4/1728."
